WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.181 --> 00:00:17.965
felt the wormhole's intense magic power pulling at him and began to panic.

2
00:00:19.025 --> 00:00:22.268
Then a strong pair of hands grabbed his shoulders.

3
00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:25.891
There was a yank, and the wormhole released him and Zing.

4
00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:31.536
He tumbled back onto the ground near the Wormwood tree, with the little dragon landing on his stomach.

5
00:00:33.104 --> 00:00:33.785
Zann grunted.

6
00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:37.747
Looking up, he saw Perda staring down at him.

7
00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:41.309
"Phew! That was close," she said.

8
00:00:44.591 --> 00:00:45.971
Darb and Gliss hurried over.

9
00:00:45.991 --> 00:00:48.453
"Good going, Perda," Darb said.

10
00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:51.955
"It looked like Zann and Zing were both going to get sucked in!"

11
00:00:51.975 --> 00:00:55.437
"We were, until Perda grabbed me," Zann admitted.

12
00:00:55.457 --> 00:00:59.959
"Thanks." "Can we get out of this creepy neighborhood now?"

13
00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:01.160
Gliss complained.

14
00:01:01.924 --> 00:01:06.746
"There's probably still time for a walk in the park or a boat ride or something nice like

15
00:01:06.806 --> 00:01:08.167
that before dinnertime."

16
00:01:08.187 --> 00:01:12.669
"Soon." Perda glanced at the huge tree.

17
00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:15.790
"I want to study the riddle a little more."

18
00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:22.713
As Zann pushed Zing off him and stood up, he noticed the itchetch creeping closer with its yellow

19
00:01:22.953 --> 00:01:24.333
eyes locked on Zing.

20
00:01:25.014 --> 00:01:27.715
The dragon spit a burst of flame at the other creature.

21
00:01:27.735 --> 00:01:30.376
"Stop it, you two," Zann scolded.

22
00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:33.955
"Or if you won't stop, at least move away from the wormhole."

23
00:01:34.795 --> 00:01:40.120
He grabbed Zing's leash and dragged the little dragon around to the opposite side of the huge tree

24
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.262
trunk. The itchetch followed.

25
00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.725
Zann released Zing and looked around.

26
00:01:45.745 --> 00:01:49.769
"I've never been to this side of the Wormwood tree before," he thought.

27
00:01:50.389 --> 00:01:54.233
Based on the rocky, rough ground, he guessed few people wandered here.

28
00:01:55.134 --> 00:02:01.346
Several large roots stuck out of the ground, and Zann noticed that one had a particularly interesting shape.

29
00:02:01.366 --> 00:02:03.106
"Come look at this, you guys!"

30
00:02:03.427 --> 00:02:03.847
he called.

31
00:02:04.747 --> 00:02:06.248
Perda appeared a moment later.

32
00:02:06.268 --> 00:02:07.688
"What is it?"

33
00:02:07.708 --> 00:02:10.009
"Where are Darb and Gliss?"

34
00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:14.592
Zann asked, stepping aside as Zing chased the itchetch past him.

35
00:02:15.472 --> 00:02:16.572
Perda rolled her eyes.

36
00:02:16.592 --> 00:02:19.394
"I don't think they heard you," she said.

37
00:02:19.414 --> 00:02:24.416
"They're looking for another flower to put in Darb's hair so the two of them will match."

38
00:02:25.528 --> 00:02:31.471
Suddenly Zann couldn't stop wondering what would happen if he tried to put a flower in Perda's hair.

39
00:02:32.271 --> 00:02:34.752
Would she like it, or would she think it was silly?

40
00:02:34.772 --> 00:02:36.693
"What did you want to show us?"

41
00:02:37.173 --> 00:02:38.894
she asked, interrupting his thoughts.

42
00:02:38.914 --> 00:02:40.835
"Check out that root."

43
00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:42.135
Zann pointed.

44
00:02:42.155 --> 00:02:44.356
"Doesn't it look like an angry troll?"

45
00:02:44.916 --> 00:02:45.677
Perda laughed.

46
00:02:46.957 --> 00:02:48.178
"Yeah, a little bit!"

47
00:02:49.038 --> 00:02:52.219
Then her smile faded, and she leaned forward.

48
00:02:53.996 --> 00:02:55.497
"Wait—do you see something in there?"

49
00:02:56.358 --> 00:03:00.821
She pointed to a hole in the root that looked like the troll's open mouth.

50
00:03:01.541 --> 00:03:04.363
Zann hadn't noticed it before, but now he did.

51
00:03:04.964 --> 00:03:09.547
The sunlight shining through the tree's branches glinted off something metallic.

52
00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:14.270
"Careful," he said as Perda crouched down for a closer look.

53
00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:18.733
"I heard that the people in Wormwood sometimes leave stuff for one another near this tree.

54
00:03:19.353 --> 00:03:21.315
Illegal stuff from other worlds, even."

55
00:03:21.335 --> 00:03:22.796
"I know."

56
00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.001
Perda stared into the hole.

57
00:03:25.021 --> 00:03:26.981
"But what if it's not that?

58
00:03:27.722 --> 00:03:30.503
The riddle says 'rooted' in one line, remember?

59
00:03:31.163 --> 00:03:34.845
Maybe that's a clue, and whatever's in the hole is important somehow."

60
00:03:35.545 --> 00:03:37.006
Zann wasn't sure about that.

61
00:03:37.686 --> 00:03:43.188
It seemed much more likely that the glinting object was an illicit stone from another world or something

62
00:03:43.228 --> 00:03:43.688
like that.

63
00:03:44.309 --> 00:03:47.350
Then again, Perda was one of the smartest people he knew.

64
00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.351
Maybe she was right.

65
00:03:49.371 --> 00:03:52.552
"Let's try to get it out, then," he said.

66
00:03:53.112 --> 00:03:54.112
"But we should be careful.

67
00:03:54.413 --> 00:03:54.933
Don't touch it."

68
00:03:55.573 --> 00:03:56.333
Perda nodded.

69
00:03:56.353 --> 00:03:59.475
"Let's try a Levitation spell to lift it out."

70
00:04:00.235 --> 00:04:03.316
She tried the spell on her own first, but nothing happened.

71
00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:08.038
So she and Zann joined their friction by rubbing their hands together.

72
00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:10.479
The metal item didn't move.

73
00:04:11.399 --> 00:04:12.860
Perda sat back on her heels.

74
00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:17.782
"We could ask Gliss to help," she said, peering around the trunk.

75
00:04:17.802 --> 00:04:22.124
"Or we could spend all day trying to figure out other spells to use.

76
00:04:22.816 --> 00:04:26.738
Or She leaned forward and stuck her hand into the hole.

77
00:04:27.959 --> 00:04:28.960
Zann bit his lip.

78
00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.521
"Perda, don't—" "Got it!"

79
00:04:32.442 --> 00:04:35.303
Perda pulled her arm out, clutching something tightly.

80
00:04:35.964 --> 00:04:40.566
At the same moment, Zann felt a shock wave of magic energy burst over him.

81
00:04:41.407 --> 00:04:43.888
He gasped and Perda's eyes went wide.

82
00:04:44.588 --> 00:04:48.571
Even Zing and the itchetch noticed and stopped chasing each other for a moment.

83
00:04:49.131 --> 00:04:49.631
"What was that?"

84
00:04:49.991 --> 00:04:50.632
Zann asked.

85
00:04:51.328 --> 00:04:52.709
"It happened right when you pulled your hand out."

86
00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:54.891
Then he gasped again.

87
00:04:54.911 --> 00:05:02.878
"Look!" A wormhole suddenly spun open at their feet, nestled between two large, gnarled roots.

88
00:05:02.898 --> 00:05:05.039
"Whoa," Perda said.

89
00:05:05.059 --> 00:05:06.721
"Is that a wormhole?

90
00:05:07.221 --> 00:05:08.923
It looks different."

91
00:05:08.943 --> 00:05:15.048
"I've never seen one on the ground before," Zann said, taking a step back from the swirling hole.

92
00:05:15.068 --> 00:05:18.210
"And how can it exist so close to the other one?

93
00:05:18.911 --> 00:05:20.092
I thought that never happened."

94
00:05:20.876 --> 00:05:22.958
Perda nodded, looking a bit pale.

95
00:05:22.978 --> 00:05:25.479
"Do you think it opened because of this?"

96
00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:30.523
She opened her hand to reveal a small, dirty scrap of metal.

97
00:05:30.543 --> 00:05:34.045
"It looks like a leaf," Zann said.

98
00:05:34.065 --> 00:05:39.148
"What if it's a powerful relic, like the Dragontamer's Charm or something like that?"

99
00:05:39.929 --> 00:05:43.391
Before Perda could answer, they both heard a loud snarl.

100
00:05:44.372 --> 00:05:47.174
Zing had just slapped the itchetch with his tail.

101
00:05:47.754 --> 00:05:51.737
The itchetch responded by leaping forward and giving the dragon a shove.

102
00:05:52.617 --> 00:05:55.798
Zing tumbled backward—right into the new wormhole!

103
00:05:55.818 --> 00:06:02.581
"Zing!" Zann shouted, barely managing to grab one of the dragon's wings before it disappeared.

104
00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:03.962
"Oh, no!

105
00:06:04.042 --> 00:06:04.742
Not again!"

106
00:06:05.142 --> 00:06:07.123
Perda cried, grabbing Zann's arm.

107
00:06:07.944 --> 00:06:10.285
Zann was relieved—but only for a second.

108
00:06:11.025 --> 00:06:16.687
Because this time, even though Perda was pulling as hard as she could, the wormhole kept sucking them

109
00:06:16.828 --> 00:06:17.528
farther in.

110
00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:24.203
"Help!" he shouted frantically as his whole arm disappeared after Zing.

111
00:06:24.223 --> 00:06:27.084
"Guys, we need help over here!"

112
00:06:27.805 --> 00:06:29.046
There was an answering shout.

113
00:06:32.628 --> 00:06:36.491
But Zann barely caught a glimpse of an alarmed-looking Darb and Gliss.

114
00:06:37.291 --> 00:06:43.415
As they appeared from around the tree, he, Zing, and Perda were sucked all the way into the

115
00:06:43.455 --> 00:06:43.975
wormhole.
